| WP8-D05 | SW2009 | T4 | `{entry} may suspend in {statement} and needs an extended task; {task} is {basic \| isr}.` |
| WP8-D06 | SW2009 | T5 | `Deadline {d} of {entry} is shorter than the response bound {r} of {task}.` |
| WP8-D07 | SW2009 | T6 | `{entry} of {occurrence} is not placed on a task of {where}; place {operation} or {occurrence} on a task, for example: {line}` / for an `after` successor whose predecessor is not on a Task that accepts it: `{entry} of {occurrence} is not placed on a task of {where}; an after successor runs on the task of its predecessor, so place {predecessor} on a task first and place {operation} with it, for example: {line} {line}` (`â€¦ so move {predecessor} to a task that also accepts {operation} and place â€¦` when the predecessor is on a Task) / `{entry} of {occurrence} is not placed on a task of {where}; {where} has no task that accepts it (it needs {requirement}), so add one and place {operation} or {occurrence} on it.` {where} is the Core of WP8-S04 (`the implicit core of {platform}` for the implicit one) or the OS node the software is deployed on. {line} is `deploy {occurrencePath}.{operation} on {taskPath};`, or `change deploy {path} on {target}; to deploy {path} on {taskPath};` when that exact path already has a deploy statement (WP8-D09). The example satisfies T2 to T5 and T7: never an ISR for an entry other than `receive`, never a periodic Task whose period does not divide the entry's, an extended Task for an entry that may suspend, no response bound above an explicit deadline, a Task of the Core the occurrence already reaches, and for an `after` successor a Task that also accepts its predecessor's entries. Among those it prefers a Task that is no ISR, then the Task that already hosts an entry of the occurrence or of its nearest ancestor, then one that accepts every unplaced entry of the occurrence, then declaration rank; an `after` successor names its predecessor's Task when that Task accepts it (review F2, verification V3). {requirement} names the kind and period, `, of kind extended` and `, with responseNs = 0 or at most {deadline}` as needed, and for an `after` successor `a task that also accepts its predecessor {predecessor}`. |
